{
  "_id": "cR7R7AExzEECUcfB",
  "name": "Cacophonic Shield",
  "type": "spell",
  "img": "icons/magic/sonic/explosion-shock-wave-teal.webp",
  "folder": "o6xVeDDtqtvcdIvb",
  "sort": 0,
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>Thunderous echoes fill a 10-foot Emanation originating from you for the duration. Whenever the Emanation enters a creature’s space, and whenever a creature enters it or ends its turn there, that creature makes a Constitution saving throw, no more than once per turn. On a failure, it takes 3d6 Thunder damage and has the &amp;Reference[deafened apply=false]{Deafened} condition until the start of your next turn; on a success, it takes half as much damage only. When you cast the spell, you can choose creatures it doesn’t affect.</p><p>You also have Resistance to Thunder damage, and ranged attack rolls against you have Disadvantage.</p><p><strong>Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.</strong> The damage increases by 1d6 for each spell slot level above 3.</p><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-PhoYQpn1GbSb4CoI\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p>The effect gives you Resistance to Thunder damage; the Disadvantage of ranged attack rolls against you is applied by hand.</p></section>",
      "chat": ""
    },
